Topic 3 — Login + Bearer usage
1) Client POST /login { username, password }
2) Server authenticates (AuthenticationManager)
3) Server builds JWT (subject, roles, expiry) and signs it
4) Client saves token
5) Later: Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOi...
6) Jwt filter verifies signature + expiry → sets SecurityContext

Session policy for APIs
http.sessionManagement(sm -&gt;
    sm.sessionCreationPolicy(SessionCreationPolicy.STATELESS)
);
Plain words: do not create an HTTP session for security. Each request must carry proof.

Topic 4 — UserDetailsService
One important method:
UserDetails loadUserByUsername(String username) throws UsernameNotFoundException;
Your implementation:

Find the user in the DB (repository)
If missing → throw UsernameNotFoundException
If found → return UserDetails wrapper

@Service
public class CustomUserDetailsService implements UserDetailsService {

    private final UserRepository users;

    public CustomUserDetailsService(UserRepository users) {
        this.users = users;
    }

    @Override
    public UserDetails loadUserByUsername(String username) {
        User user = users.findByUsername(username)
            .orElseThrow(() -&gt; new UsernameNotFoundException(username));
        return new CustomUserDetails(user);
    }
}
Security will call this during form/basic/login flows (details in lecture 37).

